# The Myth of the River of Plenty

In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a mystical river. The river had a wondrous power: any gift cast into its waters would triple before reaching the other side.

The First Village received five loaves of bread each dawn. They faced a choice: keep all five loaves, or send some across the river, trusting the Second Village to share the multiplied bounty.

At first, fear ruled. "Why should we risk our bread?" they asked. "The other village might keep everything." So they sent nothing, and both villages remained hungry.

One day, an elder said, "What if trust itself is the magic?" 

