But greed whispered in some hearts. Some kept all they received. Others sent nothing, hoping only to receive. The river still multiplied gifts, but when trust broke, both villages suffered.

The wise learned: the river's true magic wasn't multiplication—it was revealing whether humans could build bridges of trust across the waters of uncertainty. Only through reciprocity did true abundance flow.
